 multiply $7$ and $3$ without any signs: $7\\cdot 3=21.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=21.\n$$" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442413 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1069 "q-128424" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1071 "$2.2\\cdot (-4.5)=$" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1072 #uuid "c5da7489-1e96-592e-8ffe-aaecfa0d4fb2" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442437 1074 "We have the product of a positive number and a negative number, which gives a negative number.\n\n$$\n2.2\\cdot (-4.5)=-(2.2\\cdot 4.5)=-9.9\n$$" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442415 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1069 "q-180551" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1071 "$5\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=${{field-1}}" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1072 #uuid "dcae9997-c063-556b-b99d-bfc224ab7e6d" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442438 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a positive and a negative, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-3)=-15\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{5\\cdot (-3)}_{⏟}}_{-15}\\cdot 2=(-15)\\cdot 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a negative times a positive gives a negative:\n\n$$\n(-15)\\cdot 2=-(15\\cdot 2)=-30\n$$" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442417 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442439 1069 "q-128408" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442439 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442439 1071 "$(-4)\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-3)=$" 13194139534881 17592186045417 true] [17592186442439 1072 #uuid "edd9589d-5442-58a3-84f8-fb0a90d9d